# Design System: 方块星球大消除

## Overview

**Creative North Star: "把方块拼成星光"**

Softened jewel blocks sit in a low-brightness navy space. Mint identifies actions; gold carries energy, records, and rewards. Original CSS geometry, inline SVG, and canvas provide all shipped game imagery. Fonts come from the device.

This record is source-derived. Chromium launch was blocked by a sandbox shutdown syscall; no actual screenshot or layout review was achieved, and visual approval has not been recorded.

## Colors

The frontmatter records actual CSS colors. Background, Ink, and Muted establish the text hierarchy; Surface and Surface Raised are declared theme primitives, while current panels also use literal navy fills. Keep the six tile colors in source-index order. JavaScript particles use brighter feedback colors.

**The Action and Reward Rule.** Use mint for primary choices and completed states; use gold for energy, records, stars, and keyboard focus. Gem and special-block symbols use Mint Ink. Exposed ice has a light symbol; ice over an occupied tile uses the dark symbol.

## Typography

Use the installed stack: `"PingFang SC", "Microsoft YaHei", "Noto Sans CJK SC", system-ui, sans-serif`. No external font or icon-font dependency is used. Requested weights depend on the installed family; CSS disables font synthesis. Home display, score, dialog heading, and action declarations appear in the frontmatter. Page headings use (18px); game headings (16px); supporting text (9–13px). Scores and counters use tabular numerals.

## Layout

A single portrait column caps at (480px), with (22px) side padding and safe-area insets; minimum document width is (280px). Home mode cards use two columns. The square board is 8×8 with (9px) padding and (4px) gaps; the tray has three slots with (3px) piece gaps. Map routes keep the original (360 × 405) coordinates and five nodes per sector.

At widths up to (370px), side padding becomes (14px) and board padding/gaps become (7px)/(3px). At (700px) and above, a rounded portrait frame adds (30px) margins, (26px) side padding, and (820px) minimum height. At heights up to (780px) and widths up to (699px), art, scores, tray, and vertical gaps compress; game content caps at (390px). Tray JavaScript fits pieces to slot width with a (15px) tile floor and (23px), or below (780px) height (21px), ceiling.

## Elevation & Depth

Depth belongs to objects: tiles use `inset 1px 2px 0 #ffffff36, inset -1px -3px 0 #071a3936`; the board uses `0 12px 26px #080f2133`; dialogs use `0 22px 70px #0006`. Map nodes retain inset undersides, with a stronger shadow on the current node. Broad orbit rings and the shaded CSS planet remain ambient.

## Shapes

Keep tile corners (5px), standard controls (12px), tool wells (13px), icon buttons (14px), board/home cards (16px), map orbs (19px), and dialogs (22px). Planets and switch thumbs are circular. Preserve the original three-block mark, eight-point sparks, elliptical orbits, (156px) planet, and (258 × 72px) ring. Inline SVG icons use round joins/caps and (1.7) strokes; tile symbols use (1.8).

## Components

- **Buttons:** Primary and secondary dialog actions have minimum height (49px), brighter hover fills, (0.96) press scaling, and (0.42) disabled opacity. The adventure action is taller (87px; compact height 76px). Icon navigation is (44px) square. Interactive focus is a gold (3px) outline offset (4px).
- **Board and tiles:** Keep the tile bevel/facet, six fills, gem/bomb/rainbow symbols, and bordered/fractured ice. Occupied-ice symbols are (28%) wide/high at (4%) offsets with Mint Ink and full opacity. Preview borders are mint for valid, coral for invalid, gold for line clears, and purple for specials. Keyboard anchors use a white inset outline; hints describe the action.
- **Tray:** Three centered grid-shaped pieces; selection adds a mint wash/outline, empty slots show a dash, unplaceable pieces dim to (0.32), and dragging pieces to (0.18). Preserve pressed semantics and special-range labels.
- **Tools:** Bomb, shuffle, and hammer have colored (43px) wells in (80px)-wide controls, overlapping inventory badges, separate refill actions, and mint selection. Keep symbols, names, and counts together.
- **Map nodes:** Dashed routes connect current mint, cleared blue-gray, and locked dimmed orbs. Preserve the current halo, lock symbol, filled/outlined stars, names, and centered press transform.
- **Meters:** Goals combine icons, labels, numeric counts, and mint (4px) tracks; completed goals show checks. The final five moves turn orange. Energy uses a gold (5px) track, count out of six, next-special symbol, and ready-state text.
- **Dialogs and ads:** Shared dark dialog surfaces cap at (380px), scroll within the viewport, and move/trap/restore focus. Results add gold stars and large score numerals. Simulated ads keep their explicit label, original emblem, progress strip, disabled-then-ready primary action, and return action. Toasts use pale mint above the overlays.
- **Toggles:** Switches are (46 × 28px), with (20px) thumbs translating (18px); checked state changes slate to muted green. Keep the nearby label, explanation, and shared focus treatment.

Shared transitions use (180ms) and `cubic-bezier(.16, 1, .3, 1)`. Screens enter in (280ms), clears pulse in (380ms), and floating scores rise in (1100ms). Reduced-motion CSS collapses durations to (0.01ms) with one iteration; JavaScript skips canvas bursts.

## Do's and Don'ts

- **Do** preserve original code-drawn geometry, offline Chinese typography, established palette roles, and selected/preview/focus/reduced-motion states.
- **Do** review rendered home, map, board, dialogs, and compact layouts when browser capture is available.
- **Don't** introduce external fonts, dependencies, network imagery, or borrowed game artwork.
- **Don't** remove distinguishing symbols and dark gem/special/occupied-ice strokes, or describe source checks as screenshot validation or visual approval.
